From e6f92d3c39c4f6402b4088b0cd7da2f139a73f2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sandeep Tomer <stomer@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 15:26:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] [prplmesh] CURE reported issues Fix.

crash/overflow guards and buffer-safety issues in monitoring, TLV parsing, and TC filters
- Add divide-by-zero, null-pointer, and bounds checks in monitor_db,
  link metrics tasks, and netlink stats parsing
- Fix TLVF alloc_*() functions to update length/index counters only
  after buffer bounds checks succeed, and add overflow guards on
  count/length fields
- Fix inverted alloc() success check in steering policy TLV construction
- Validate interface names before use in tc shell commands (command
  injection hardening)
- Clean up orphaned DM instance on AgentDisconnectedEvent setup failure
.

Signed-off-by: Sandeep Tomer <stomer@qti.qualcomm.com>
